 "reading": [
  "T1 is an upper bound: 5G derives fresh AS keys at handover from the existing KAMF-rooted context (TS 33.501 \u00a76.9.2.1.1, SECONDARY) and the PDU session persists; an application-layer PQ re-handshake per handover only happens if the transport session is torn down.",
  "Even so, for a 3 kb/s wearable ECG the per-handover full-PQ bound exceeds the stream itself at highway handover rates (see T1_share_of_stream_pct); DTLS CID (RFC 9146/9147) and PSK resumption (RFC 9846 \u00a72.2) are the mechanisms that keep sessions across address changes.",
  "Every RTT anchor exceeds the 2 ms local-surgery budget by an order of magnitude and the LEO RTD exceeds the 20 ms remote budget: no key establishment can sit inside a URLLC control loop; it must be pre-established and rekeyed symmetrically."
 ]
}